WEBVTT

00:23.820 --> 00:26.440
<i>It's mating season for the scalewolves.</i>

00:27.310 --> 00:30.260
<i>They shed their plaitscale fur 
through sharp impacts</i>

00:30.260 --> 00:34.370
<i>to prevent harm to 
their coming offspring.</i>

00:35.590 --> 00:40.300
<i>Even though they could stay as strong as 
they are if they chose not to mate...</i>

00:44.070 --> 00:47.320
<i>I thought that I had 
nothing to learn from her.</i>

00:48.490 --> 00:50.750
<i>That Outsiders don't belong here.</i>

00:50.750 --> 00:53.800
<i>That they have nothing 
to offer the world of magic.</i>

00:55.570 --> 00:56.710
<i>But...</i>

00:57.420 --> 01:00.180
<i>If she correctly learns 
how everything works...</i>

01:00.590 --> 01:04.700
<i>How is she any different from us?</i>

02:43.560 --> 02:45.770
Yes! I did it!

02:45.770 --> 02:47.570
Excellent work!

02:45.940 --> 02:51.150
<b>The Test in Serpentback Cave</b>

02:48.200 --> 02:51.650
You've learned how to draw 
your spells very reliably, Coco.

02:51.650 --> 02:53.130
I'm so happy!

02:54.160 --> 02:55.530
But...

02:55.530 --> 02:59.520
There aren't many spells 
I'm fully confident in.

02:59.520 --> 03:03.050
I'll probably end up falling 
back on the same seals.

03:04.990 --> 03:06.900
If you ask me...

03:07.350 --> 03:12.170
spells you can complete consistently 
and draw without much effort

03:12.550 --> 03:14.780
are what I'd call your specialty.

03:18.450 --> 03:21.280
My... specialty?

03:23.520 --> 03:24.640
See?

03:24.640 --> 03:28.860
The spells you use most often are 
the ones that use more straight lines.

03:29.330 --> 03:33.820
Your straight lines are much 
more confident than your curves.

03:34.560 --> 03:39.380
The first time we met, you were 
drawing straight lines, remember?

03:41.650 --> 03:44.130
Realizing which spells are your specialty

03:44.130 --> 03:48.460
will give you confidence when 
you need to believe in yourself.

03:49.410 --> 03:51.340
When you're feeling nervous, 
say it out loud,

03:51.340 --> 03:53.600
so your own ears can hear it.

03:55.730 --> 03:59.920
My specialty is... drawing straight lines.

04:00.690 --> 04:04.220
My specialty is straight lines, right?!

04:04.540 --> 04:07.080
Now that I know, I should 
draw more straight lines!

04:07.480 --> 04:10.180
I'll charge <i>straight</i> into success!

04:10.180 --> 04:11.730
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

04:12.790 --> 04:16.040
You'll master your specialty 
spells without even trying.

04:16.990 --> 04:19.560
Better to practice spells 
you haven't perfected yet,

04:20.570 --> 04:23.040
that you need active work to pin down.

04:23.490 --> 04:26.580
It could even lead you to new specialties.

04:27.510 --> 04:28.570
Right?

04:29.440 --> 04:31.250
R-Right...

04:36.340 --> 04:41.060
<i>Casting Seals seem even more 
impressive to me now than before.</i>

04:46.520 --> 04:51.820
<i>Now that I know how they work,</i>

04:52.760 --> 04:56.140
<i>I appreciate how hard they 
must have been to design.</i>

04:58.020 --> 05:01.830
Amazing. This is amazing!

05:01.830 --> 05:03.810
The magic of amazing people is amazing!

05:03.810 --> 05:06.790
She needs to improve her 
compliment vocabulary.

05:07.400 --> 05:10.670
I feel amazingly intimidated 
by the amazingness...

05:10.670 --> 05:12.540
Want to look with me, Richeh?

05:13.720 --> 05:14.820
No.

05:17.270 --> 05:21.080
I like drawing. I don't like looking.

05:21.840 --> 05:23.900
Really? You don't want to look at this?

05:23.900 --> 05:27.110
You'll learn so much!

05:23.900 --> 05:27.110
Seriously, no. And stop wiggling around.

05:30.050 --> 05:34.390
Studying magic isn't all about 
training your hands, Richeh.

05:36.030 --> 05:40.440
Looking at the advanced spells 
of others will train your eyes to—

05:40.440 --> 05:42.000
I don't want to!

05:43.200 --> 05:45.240
Richeh! You okay?

05:45.240 --> 05:46.550
Were you hurt?

05:48.340 --> 05:51.370
You really shouldn't 
cast while you're upset.

05:51.370 --> 05:52.640
That's really dangerous.

05:57.730 --> 05:59.140
Wait, Richeh!

06:03.800 --> 06:06.720
When you close your eyes 
to the guideposts of learning...

06:07.070 --> 06:09.720
and shut your ears to 
the words of your teacher...

06:10.850 --> 06:13.350
you'll go nowhere fast.

06:18.790 --> 06:19.900
Richeh!

06:21.020 --> 06:23.360
Um... I'm sorry about what I said.

06:24.020 --> 06:25.220
I...

06:29.340 --> 06:31.550
Huh? Richeh?

06:32.690 --> 06:34.120
She's not here?

06:36.340 --> 06:38.040
Maybe she's in her bedroom?

06:43.550 --> 06:45.820
Brushbuddy, do you know where she is?

06:52.980 --> 06:54.640
Where are you going, Brushbuddy?!

07:06.860 --> 07:08.110
Brushbuddy?

07:08.660 --> 07:11.160
What is this place?

07:38.960 --> 07:41.060
I didn't say you could come in.

07:41.060 --> 07:44.250
S-Sorry. I was following 
Brushbuddy, and...

07:44.250 --> 07:46.520
What a beautiful spell!

07:46.520 --> 07:48.820
It's like ribbons made out of crystal...

07:52.580 --> 07:54.400
It doesn't have a name yet.

07:54.810 --> 07:56.080
I made it myself.

07:56.080 --> 07:58.210
You made a spell?!

07:58.650 --> 08:01.210
Wow! That's amazing!

08:02.090 --> 08:05.400
It's so beautiful! 
It makes my eyes happy!

08:05.400 --> 08:07.640
What an avant-garde 
show of appreciation...

08:09.670 --> 08:13.090
I really love this spell.

08:20.400 --> 08:22.440
You can have one if you want.

08:22.900 --> 08:24.270
I've got plenty.

08:24.270 --> 08:25.780
What?! Really?!

08:28.410 --> 08:31.140
I love it! Thank you!

08:33.240 --> 08:37.200
Hey... can I ask something?

08:38.500 --> 08:41.070
Why don't you want to look at the books?

08:43.240 --> 08:46.460
I know so little about magic,

08:46.460 --> 08:48.770
so I love looking at 
other people's spells.

08:50.050 --> 08:54.670
Who could have made them, 
what did they use them for...

08:54.670 --> 08:58.270
I love imagining that stuff 
as I look through their spells.

09:02.970 --> 09:07.230
I only want to think about my own spells.

09:09.610 --> 09:11.360
If I start looking at books,

09:11.360 --> 09:15.740
they'll start telling me 
to draw what's in there.

09:16.230 --> 09:18.980
I'll have to draw things 
I don't want to draw.

09:18.980 --> 09:21.250
Stuff that isn't my style of spell.

09:22.150 --> 09:24.170
I'm sick of that.

09:24.170 --> 09:25.360
Richeh...

09:26.380 --> 09:28.660
It has nothing to do with you.

09:29.440 --> 09:31.930
I don't need other people's spells.

09:31.930 --> 09:35.170
I don't want them to contaminate mine.

09:36.780 --> 09:43.040
Richeh was apprenticed to another 
witch before she came here.

09:43.520 --> 09:47.300
She uses her stubbornness 
as a shield to protect herself.

09:47.690 --> 09:51.260
Like a scalewolf making 
armor out of its thick fur...

09:51.720 --> 09:53.740
I'm never sure how much to interfere.

09:55.370 --> 09:59.430
Unfortunately, people 
aren't as simple as spells.

10:01.260 --> 10:02.320
Here.

10:02.320 --> 10:03.460
What's this?

10:06.140 --> 10:07.420
Stones?

10:07.420 --> 10:11.170
My latest creation: Snugstones.

10:11.490 --> 10:13.650
It's meant as a sleep aid.

10:13.650 --> 10:17.800
Put one under the covers and 
it'll warm you from tip to toe.

10:17.800 --> 10:21.610
Might just be a placebo, but 
give them out to your apprentices.

10:22.800 --> 10:23.940
Thank you.

10:24.770 --> 10:27.190
There's so much kindness in your spells.

10:27.850 --> 10:29.570
You express it better
 with magic than words.

10:29.570 --> 10:32.740
Th-This is just part of 
my work, you get that?!

10:32.740 --> 10:37.200
I intend to sell them, 
so I'm looking for feedback!

10:37.560 --> 10:39.950
Sure, let's not argue.

10:45.810 --> 10:46.770
Hey, Olly.

10:47.840 --> 10:49.250
You gave me too many.

10:49.250 --> 10:50.340
There are five here.

10:52.190 --> 10:53.990
Four are for your apprentices.

10:55.560 --> 10:57.970
The last one is for you.

11:00.020 --> 11:03.240
Set an example for the girls 
and get a good night's sleep.

11:06.150 --> 11:07.560
You're a teacher, remember?

11:14.140 --> 11:15.530
I'll try.

11:19.500 --> 11:20.840
A letter?

11:21.310 --> 11:22.560
From whom?

11:26.470 --> 11:28.400
I'm back.

11:29.800 --> 11:30.900
Agott.

11:32.000 --> 11:34.330
You arrived at the perfect time.

11:34.820 --> 11:36.760
I just received word from the Great Hall.

11:37.200 --> 11:39.400
We have a date for your second test.

11:40.070 --> 11:41.330
When is it?!

11:41.640 --> 11:43.580
Morning, three days from now...

11:44.600 --> 11:47.840
at Serpentback Cave in Cape Romonon.

11:56.430 --> 11:59.160
You're trying to make crystal ribbons?

12:00.990 --> 12:04.240
That's a very charming spell, Richehlette.

12:16.170 --> 12:17.550
Look, Rili.

12:19.880 --> 12:22.680
It's sparkly and roly-poly. Is it pretty?

12:33.830 --> 12:35.260
Rili?

12:36.440 --> 12:37.960
Richeh, your big brother...

12:38.370 --> 12:41.530
loves it when you make spells 
that express who you are.

12:43.370 --> 12:47.200
Never stop being yourself, okay?

12:49.450 --> 12:50.710
Rili?

12:51.610 --> 12:52.980
Where are you going?

12:53.530 --> 12:56.710
You don't wanna look 
at my spells anymore?

12:57.030 --> 12:58.350
Don't go...

12:58.690 --> 12:59.960
Rili!

13:07.090 --> 13:08.260
A dream?

13:09.830 --> 13:13.350
Ugh, I fell fast asleep!

13:13.810 --> 13:17.860
I meant to use every minute I had 
to practice before the test!

13:18.260 --> 13:20.120
This stupid Snugstone!

13:20.120 --> 13:22.180
Stupid toasty warmth!

13:23.630 --> 13:25.290
You'll be all right, Agott.

13:25.900 --> 13:30.080
Everyone always feels like 
they haven't prepared enough.

13:30.950 --> 13:33.080
Just approach it as 
the person you are now.

13:34.220 --> 13:36.590
That will serve the person 
you'll be the next time.

13:40.090 --> 13:42.090
There won't be a next time.

13:48.630 --> 13:50.850
I'll pass the test on the first try.

13:50.850 --> 13:53.410
I'm from House Arklaum, after all.

13:53.410 --> 13:56.290
Such heartening words!

13:58.270 --> 14:01.610
Like night and day with 
my little failure here.

14:01.610 --> 14:03.550
Euini, my apprentice,

14:03.550 --> 14:06.990
has tried and failed the 
second test twice already,

14:06.990 --> 14:10.000
even though you can 
only take it once a year!

14:10.310 --> 14:15.300
If only I could trade him for 
a daughter of House Arklaum!

14:15.300 --> 14:16.630
Master Kukrow.

14:16.630 --> 14:20.520
Apprentices aren't things. 
We can't simply trade them around...

14:20.520 --> 14:22.590
Ah, but don't you wish we could?

14:23.300 --> 14:25.640
We can't repair them, either!

14:25.980 --> 14:27.650
How dare you—

14:27.650 --> 14:29.770
I-It's fine.

14:30.520 --> 14:32.870
It's all true, anyway.

14:32.870 --> 14:37.690
My incompetence as an apprentice has 
given Master Kukrow no end of trouble.

14:37.690 --> 14:38.520
Um...

14:38.520 --> 14:40.510
And I'm sorry that my incompetence

14:40.510 --> 14:43.630
has splashed back into criticism 
against you again, Master.

14:43.630 --> 14:47.110
I'm also sorry I'll probably never 
become a worthy witch...

14:44.440 --> 14:46.590
Um... Euini?

14:47.110 --> 14:49.680
Hey, sorry I'm late.

14:50.040 --> 14:53.410
The closest Windowway has become unusable,

14:53.410 --> 14:56.920
so I had to walk all the way here.

14:58.450 --> 15:01.920
That enormous brushbuddy is talking!

15:02.380 --> 15:04.010
Look closer.

15:04.010 --> 15:06.990
She's a proper witch.

15:07.280 --> 15:08.050
What?

15:08.050 --> 15:10.560
But transformation is 
forbidden magic, isn't it?

15:11.010 --> 15:13.410
A Mirror Cloak of Borrowshade.

15:13.800 --> 15:15.810
A magical contraption that,

15:15.810 --> 15:19.910
while worn, projects an illusionary 
guise of a nearby beast.

15:20.990 --> 15:23.800
It's a pleasure to meet you. I'm Alaira.

15:23.800 --> 15:28.070
I'll be overseeing your participation 
in the second test.

15:28.450 --> 15:30.480
So you're the test proctor?

15:30.480 --> 15:32.160
Purely a coincidence!

15:32.160 --> 15:33.630
And you brought all your apprentices,

15:33.630 --> 15:35.460
even though they're 
not all taking the test?

15:36.490 --> 15:39.280
The second test, 
the Sincerity of the Shield—

15:39.280 --> 15:43.410
as the name suggests, you become 
like a knight with a shield,

15:43.410 --> 15:45.970
keeping your target safe as you 
escort them from the entrance

15:45.970 --> 15:48.590
to the exit of the Serpentback Cave.

15:48.590 --> 15:51.420
You mustn't lose sight of 
your charge during that time.

15:51.420 --> 15:55.440
If either reaches the cave 
exit alone, you're out.

15:55.440 --> 15:59.860
Of course, you fail if you're 
witnessed casting spells, as well.

15:59.860 --> 16:03.110
What happens if we're witnessed?

16:03.110 --> 16:05.730
There's no risk of the secrets 
of magic getting out,

16:05.730 --> 16:08.110
but you will fail the test...

16:08.720 --> 16:11.020
because you'll be exposed as human.

16:11.020 --> 16:14.490
Put those cloaks on and have a look.

16:25.690 --> 16:28.130
Are those gryphons?

16:28.130 --> 16:30.910
No, they're myrphons.

16:30.910 --> 16:32.890
A different species 
that lives by the water.

16:33.740 --> 16:36.160
The Serpentback Cave, 
where the test takes place,

16:36.160 --> 16:39.030
is a magical ruin from 
a more tumultuous age.

16:39.030 --> 16:41.480
A labyrinth spell pervades its caverns,

16:41.480 --> 16:44.080
making it dangerous 
to stray from the path.

16:45.510 --> 16:51.280
So the second test is about using 
magic to protect them <i>from</i> magic?

16:51.280 --> 16:52.810
That's right!

16:52.810 --> 16:55.720
Humans rarely enter the ruins,

16:55.720 --> 16:59.430
but it's been a route between 
the animals' breeding grounds

16:59.430 --> 17:01.290
and winter nests for ages now.

17:01.290 --> 17:05.550
We witches must take responsibility 
for altering their environment.

17:08.570 --> 17:09.970
That's why, every year,

17:09.970 --> 17:13.110
we guide and protect the young ones 
making the trip for the first time

17:13.110 --> 17:16.770
to keep them from going astray.

17:16.770 --> 17:22.650
With those cloaks on, the myrphons 
will see you as one of their own.

17:22.650 --> 17:24.930
If you take the cloaks off 
or disrupt their seal,

17:24.930 --> 17:27.590
the myrphons will run away, 
so be careful!

17:28.150 --> 17:29.650
<i>I see.</i>

17:29.650 --> 17:35.660
<i>In a way, this is harder than drawing 
spells without humans seeing us.</i>

17:36.260 --> 17:38.410
You'll each be in charge of one myrphon.

17:38.910 --> 17:40.660
This one is yours.

17:40.660 --> 17:42.200
This one is yours.

17:42.940 --> 17:45.420
And the last one...

17:45.420 --> 17:46.540
Here you go.

17:49.450 --> 17:50.680
Richeh gets one?

17:51.490 --> 17:53.620
You've made a mistake.

17:53.620 --> 17:55.720
I'm not taking the test.

17:56.120 --> 17:58.320
What? You aren't?

17:58.320 --> 17:59.860
You submitted an application.

17:59.860 --> 18:01.680
There's no mistake.

18:02.020 --> 18:05.190
You'll be taking the test too, Richeh.

18:15.750 --> 18:17.200
You liar.

18:17.570 --> 18:18.770
Richeh...

18:20.200 --> 18:22.040
Master Qifrey,

18:22.040 --> 18:24.990
you said I could do what I wanted.

18:25.670 --> 18:28.160
That's why I came to you 
in the first place.

18:28.730 --> 18:31.810
I guess you don't care 
about what I want, either.

18:31.810 --> 18:34.720
Adults all just force you 
to do what they want.

18:35.670 --> 18:38.220
I absolutely do care what you want.

18:38.680 --> 18:43.230
That's precisely the reason 
I want you to take the test.

18:43.830 --> 18:48.780
I think that what you learn here will 
empower you in the life you want to live.

18:49.220 --> 18:50.370
So...

18:51.720 --> 18:54.420
Won't you please trust me this one time?

19:01.970 --> 19:05.420
I'm going to do what I want on the test.

19:06.880 --> 19:07.780
Okay.

19:08.240 --> 19:10.250
Okay. That's fine.

19:10.760 --> 19:13.880
If I try it and hate it, 
I'm not doing it again.

19:14.530 --> 19:20.350
And if it makes me stop being me, 
I'll never trust what you say again!

19:24.810 --> 19:28.310
Sounds like you have 
quite a handful yourself.

19:28.310 --> 19:31.600
There really is no correcting 
fools like that.

19:31.600 --> 19:34.630
They just complain and make 
excuses. "Oh, but Master!"

19:36.570 --> 19:39.370
It really is a chore.

19:39.370 --> 19:40.690
Why must children be so—

19:40.690 --> 19:41.950
Excuse me.

19:42.430 --> 19:45.210
Were you saying something?

19:47.430 --> 19:52.020
Well, would you look at the time? 
I really must return to the Great Hall.

19:54.360 --> 19:57.140
You're not going to stick around 
for your apprentice's test?

19:58.080 --> 20:01.170
You two can handle it, can't you?

20:01.170 --> 20:04.160
So get to it!

20:07.640 --> 20:10.540
Unbelievable! He really did leave!

20:11.490 --> 20:12.730
Euini...

20:13.050 --> 20:15.530
I-I'll do my best!

20:15.530 --> 20:18.390
R-Right. Please do...

20:24.510 --> 20:26.140
It's just about time.

20:26.620 --> 20:30.670
<i>May they all reach the end 
without getting lost in the dark.</i>

20:31.000 --> 20:32.750
<i>That's what magic is for.</i>

20:32.750 --> 20:34.450
<i>For just that...</i>

20:45.010 --> 20:46.770
The migration has begun.

20:58.320 --> 21:00.140
All right, let's move out!

21:22.250 --> 21:23.800
There they go.

21:24.110 --> 21:27.620
Well, let's have ourselves 
a late breakfast.

21:27.620 --> 21:29.630
I'll tell you some history, too.

21:29.930 --> 21:31.490
History?

21:31.490 --> 21:37.980
Yes, you don't know much about magical 
ruins like the Serpentback Cave, do you?

21:40.320 --> 21:44.060
Forbidden spells drawn 
before the Day of the Pact...

21:45.800 --> 21:48.400
still linger across the world like scars.

21:50.460 --> 21:53.460
W-We have to take this road?

21:53.460 --> 21:55.050
Didn't you say it?

21:55.050 --> 21:57.960
It's a test about using magic 
to protect against magic.

21:58.740 --> 22:01.340
Now, my little magic 
shield-wielding knights...

22:01.340 --> 22:04.520
How will you traverse this road?

23:35.390 --> 23:40.060
Episode 12:

23:35.390 --> 23:40.060
The Shadow of Romonon
